  "_comment": [
    "Phase 0 migration map — the geo, blog and page portion.",
    "",
    "Pulled from the live WordPress sitemap index on 31 Aug 2026:",
    "  sitemap-posttype-service-area.xml   99 URLs",
    "  sitemap-posttype-post.2026.xml      39 URLs",
    "  sitemap-posttype-post.2025.xml      14 URLs",
    "  sitemap-posttype-post.2024.xml      14 URLs",
    "  sitemap-posttype-post.2023.xml       9 URLs",
    "  sitemap-posttype-page.xml           27 URLs (includes the site root)",
    "  sitemap-posttype-service.xml        39 URLs",
    "                                     ---",
    "                                     241 rows, of which /commercial-pest-control/",
    "                                     appears in two sitemaps, so 240 unique paths.",
    "",
    "NOTE ON THE COUNT: the original audit recorded 242. The sitemap as pulled",
    "today yields 240 unique paths. We record what was measured rather than what",
    "was remembered; `live` below is that measurement and is the thing the",
    "coverage check runs against.",
    "",
    "SERVICE URLs are NOT listed in `map`. They are generated from the legacy[]",
    "arrays in services.ts and from RETIRED_TO_EXCLUSION, so the 39-to-23",
    "consolidation and the redirect table cannot drift apart. scripts/",
    "redirects.mjs merges the two halves, checks for chains, duplicate sources",
    "and self-loops, and reconciles the result against `live`.",
    "",
    "PATHS UNCHANGED between the old site and the new one are listed under",
    "`unchanged` rather than under `map`. They need no rule; they are recorded",
    "so the inventory reconciles to completion rather than to approximately.",
    "",
    "NEIGHBORHOOD URLs for neighborhoods that did not earn a page under the",
    "capacity gate (owner sign-off, 30 Aug 2026) go to their town page, which",
    "names them in the copy. That is deliberate: a redirect to a page that",
    "mentions the place beats a thin page existing only to catch the URL.",
    "",
    "TOWNS WE DO NOT SERVICE (La Conner, Anacortes, the islands, Point Roberts)",
    "go to their county page, which names them and says plainly that we do not",
    "run them. Sending that traffic to a booking page would waste the visitor's",
    "time and ours.",
    "",
    "2 Sep 2026: `gallery` moved from `map` to `unchanged`. The old site had a",
    "/gallery/ page and this map sent it to /about/, which was right until the",
    "new site grew a real /gallery/ — at which point the rule shadowed it and",
    "the page 308-redirected away from itself. redirects.mjs now fails on any",
    "rule whose source collides with a built page, so this cannot recur silently."
  ],
